          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A game requires one token per roll of a fair six-sided die. If the die lands on a six, the game is won. Otherwise, the game is lost and another token is needed to roll again.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p26-q31-request",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What is the least number of tokens Bob needs so that he has at least a 95% chance of winning at least once?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p26-q31-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "17 tokens.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p26-q31-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use the complement of losing every roll; 16 rolls fall below 95%, whereas 17 reach the threshold.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "For $n$ independent rolls, the complementary event is rolling no sixes.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{at least one win in }n\\text{ rolls})&=1-P(\\text{no sixes in }n\\text{ rolls})\\\\P(\\text{at least one win in }n\\text{ rolls})&=1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n\\\\P(\\text{at least one win in }16\\text{ rolls})&=1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^{16}\\\\P(\\text{at least one win in }16\\text{ rolls})&\\approx0.9459<0.95\\\\P(\\text{at least one win in }17\\text{ rolls})&=1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^{17}\\\\P(\\text{at least one win in }17\\text{ rolls})&\\approx0.9549>0.95\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe probability increases with the number of rolls, so the least number required is **17 tokens**.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 78
  },
